zen - severely limits model capacity", "body": "Cell 15: `for name, parameter in model.bert.named_parameters(): parameter.requires_grad = False`. The entire BERT backbone is frozen, only the classification head trains. This prevents the model from adapting representations to the disaster tweet task.", "confidence": 0.9}, {"title": "Attention mask moved to CPU causing device mismatch during inference", "body": "Cell 17: `inputs['attention_mask'] = inputs['attention_mask'].cpu()`. This moves attention_mask to CPU while input_ids and token_type_ids are on GPU via `.to(model.device)`. Passing `**inputs` to the model causes a RuntimeError due to tensors on different devices.", "confidence": 0.9}, {"title": "Test DataLoader has shuffle=True misaligning predictions with IDs", "body": "Cell 17: `test_dataloader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(test_dataset, batch_size=64, shuffle=True)`. Shuffling changes prediction order. Then `test_df['target'] = predictions` assigns shuffled predictions back to original rows, misaligning predictions with tweet IDs.", "confidence": 0.9}, {"title": "Data leakage: 128 validation samples copied to training set", "body": "Cell 11: `train_texts = pd.concat([train_texts, val_texts.iloc[:128]])` moves 128 val samples to train. These same samples remain in val_dataset, so the model sees validation data during training, inflating metrics.", "confidence": 0.9}, {"title": "greater_is_better not set for F1 metric in TrainingArguments", "body": "Cell 15, TrainingArguments: `metric_for_best_model='f1'` but `greater_is_better` is not set. Trainer defaults to `greater_is_better=False`, so it tries to MINIMIZE F1. With `load_best_model_at_end=True`, it loads the WORST model.", "confidence": 0.9}, {"title": "Randomized label dataset created but never used", "body": "Cell 15: `randomized_label_dataset = SentimentDataset(...)` creates a dataset with shuffled labels, but `trainer.evaluate(eval_dataset=val_dataset)` evaluates on the original unshuffled val_datase